l,"result":"I've migrated `editorDataMemory.js` to TypeScript and moved the backend interfaces into a new types file. All three acceptance commands pass: `tsc` reports no errors, the unit tests pass (554 passed, 1 skipped), and `lint:check` shows 0 errors. Its one warning is in `AdminPanel/.../useAiPlugin.js` and has nothing to do with this change. The work is committed as `9c30d7f`.\n\n**What changed**\n- I moved `DocService/sources/editorDataMemory.js` to `.ts` with `git mv`. `EditorCommon`, `EditorData` and `EditorStat` are now ES classes, typed strictly inside and with `unknown` for outside input. The modules it requires that have no types get a small local interface for the part it uses. It still uses CommonJS, and `module.exports = {EditorData, EditorStat}` is the same as before.\n- New file `DocService/sources/editorData.types.ts` holds only types: `EditorDataContract`, `EditorStatContract`, a shared `EditorCommonContract`, and the value shapes they use. The two classes `implements` them.\n- `.gitignore` and `.prettierignore` list the emitted `editorDataMemory.js`, and the old `.js` is no longer tracked.\n\n**Decisions**\n1. **Interface names:** they are called `*Contract` because `EditorData` and `EditorStat` are already the exported class names.\n2. **Two ignore lines, not one:** the packet asked for one line per emitted file, but `ts-strip.js` also writes `editorData.types.js` from the new types file. I listed that one too, so it doesn't show up as an untracked file or get flagged by Prettier.\n3. **Classes instead of prototype functions:** every caller uses `new`, so this is safe. There are two small runtime differences: the classes can't be called without `new`, and their methods are no longer enumerable. `EditorCommon` isn't exported, so nothing outside the file can subclass it the old way.\n4. **Existing bug kept as is:** in `setEditorConnections`, the loop compares a whole stats entry to a number instead of its `.time`. That comparison is always false, so old entries are never trimmed. I kept it, with a cast and a comment, because fixing it would change behavior. It deserves its own packet, but I didn't create one because this run doesn't allow writes under `.theseus/queue/`.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas** (I couldn't record them in the packet, the Atlas or `friction.jsonl` from this run)\n- A types-only `.ts` file still produces an emitted `.js`, so the \"one ignore line per migrated file\" rule should become \"one per emitted file\".\n- `import('./x.types')` type queries without an extension work under `nodenext` for CommonJS.\n- Turning prototype code into classes is safe only when every caller uses `new`. Check that before converting.\n- Migrations can surface hidden bugs, like the comparison above. The rule should be to keep them, mark them in a comment, and spawn a separate packet.","ttft_ms":2105,"type":"result","duration_ms":167627,"uuid":"22eceb41-b749-4f06-be7e-42feb1976b0a","ttft_stream_ms":1057,"time_to_request_ms":403,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":4,"system_prompt":231,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":28,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":9,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":8,"init_frame_send":8,"engine_pickup":8,"loop_entry":5,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":3,"request_announcements":13,"query_setup":4,"auto_mode_context_wait":17,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":32,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":8,"request_build":14},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":66,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":221,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":215,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":139,"process_rss_mib_result":232,"process_anon_mib_result":140,"process_peak_rss_mib":252,"process_cpu_ms_turn":3846,"process_wall_ms_turn":167627,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":2177,"process_wall_ms_streaming":111602,"main_stream_count":15,"main_stream_event_count":2278,"main_stream_